<article class="post">
<header class="post-header wrap-narrow">
  <span class="eyebrow">Vector search · Benchmarks</span>
  <h1><%= post["title"] %></h1>
  <p class="post-meta"><time datetime="<%= post["date"] %>"><%= post["display_date"] %></time> · <%= post["read_minutes"] %> min read</p>
  <p class="post-lede">After documents, graphs, time series and columns, vectors. We loaded a million embeddings into SoliDB, PostgreSQL with pgvector and LanceDB, and measured each search twice: how often it finds the true nearest neighbours, then how fast. The first run found two bugs in SoliDB that made its recall stop near 0.6 whatever we asked of it. This is what they were, what replaced them, and where the two others are still ahead.</p>
  <p class="post-note">Every figure on this page was measured on November 18, 2026 on one machine. pgvector ran in a container with 4 cores and 16 GB; SoliDB and LanceDB ran under the same limits in a systemd scope (the same cores, the same memory ceiling, no swap), and the harness on other cores. SoliDB is a build of <code>main</code> after 2.14.0; nothing here is in a release yet.</p>
</header>
<div class="wrap-narrow"><%- partial("blog/cover", {"post": post, "css_class": "post-cover", "loading": "eager"}) %></div>

<div class="post-body wrap-narrow">
<nav class="post-toc" aria-label="In this post">
  <p class="post-toc-title">In this post</p>
  <ol>
    <li><a href="#what">What was measured</a></li>
    <li><a href="#results">The results</a></li>
    <li><a href="#before">Where 2.14.0 stood</a></li>
    <li><a href="#changed">What changed</a></li>
