</nav>

<section id="what"><h2>What was measured</h2>
<p>The data is generated: 1,000,000 vectors of 128 dimensions, drawn around 100 centres and normalised, as embeddings are clustered and usually normalised. Each vector carries an integer <code>id</code> and a category <code>cat</code>, one of ten. 500 query vectors are drawn the same way, apart from the data. Before anything is timed, the harness computes the exact ten nearest neighbours of every query by brute force, once over all the vectors and once over each query's category.</p>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Scenario</th><th>What one request asks</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>search</code></td><td>The ten vectors nearest to a query (cosine).</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>filtered</code></td><td>The ten nearest among those of one category: a filter that a tenth of the vectors pass.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p>All three build an HNSW graph with the same settings, 16 links a node and a candidate list of 200 while building, and are searched at three widths, <code>ef</code> 40, 100 and 200: the number of candidates a search keeps, which trades speed for recall. Each width is measured twice. First <strong>recall@10</strong>: the share of the true ten nearest that the answer contains, over the 500 queries. Then requests per second and latency, at one client and at eight, the median of three runs of ten seconds. A search that is faster but finds fewer of the right answers is not faster at the same thing, so the two are always read together here.</p>
<p>SoliDB receives <code>VECTOR_SEARCH</code> in SDBQL over its native driver, on documents <code>{id, cat, emb}</code> with an HNSW index on <code>emb</code>. PostgreSQL 17 with pgvector holds a table <code>items(id, cat, emb vector(128))</code>, an HNSW index with <code>vector_cosine_ops</code> built after the load as pgvector advises, an index on <code>cat</code>, and <code>hnsw.iterative_scan = relaxed_order</code> so that a filtered search still returns ten rows. LanceDB 0.41 is a library: it runs in its client's process, with no server and no network, and was used that way, from Python, with an <code>IVF_HNSW_SQ</code> index and a prefilter on <code>cat</code>.</p>
</section>

